        <mxCell id="c29" value="s1 (A&amp;#8211;B)" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;fontColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="250" y="84" width="100" height="22" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c30" value="s2 (A&amp;#8211;C)" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;fontColor=#4d7a38;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="250" y="354" width="100" height="22" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c31" value="s3 (B&amp;#8211;C)" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;fontColor=#b07a00;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="435" y="232" width="90" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c32" value="feed-through net&lt;br&gt;A &amp;#8594; B &amp;#8594; C" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#0050ef;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="462" y="120" width="130" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c33" value="&amp;#9472;&amp;#9472; 2-pin net crossing a boundary &amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;font color='#0050ef'&gt;- - -&lt;/font&gt; feed-through net: enters B through s1 and leaves through s3, so it takes demand on &lt;b&gt;both&lt;/b&gt; segments&lt;br&gt;Thick coloured lines = boundary segments (red = over capacity)" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="364" width="480" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c34" value="&lt;b&gt;1. Segment.&lt;/b&gt; A maximal stretch of boundary between one pair of adjacent regions. A pair can own several segments (rectilinear regions), so capacity is kept per segment, not per pair.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Capacity&lt;/b&gt; $$C_s$$ = routing tracks that cross the segment. Extracted once before GP from OpenROAD's GCell capacities (fallback: $$\rho\cdot\ell$$ from LEF track pitch). One crossing net uses one track.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Demand&lt;/b&gt; $$D_s$$ = nets crossing the segment (a soft, differentiable count in GP). A feed-through net counts on its entry &lt;i&gt;and&lt;/i&gt; exit segments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. Penalty&lt;/b&gt; (GrandPlan Eq.5 shape): zero while under capacity, steep once over&lt;br&gt;$$d_s=\frac{D_s-C_s}{C_s},\quad L_{cap}=\sum_s \left(2[d_s]_+^3+[d_s]_+^2\right)$$Turned on at overflow &amp;#8804; 0.30 and kept on after the freeze. The evaluator reports per-segment utilisation $$D_s/C_s$$ as a hard check." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="620" y="90" width="520" height="420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c35" value="&lt;b&gt;Worked example&lt;/b&gt; (capacities made up for illustration)&lt;br&gt;&lt;table border='1' cellpadding='4' style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px;font-family:Times New Roman'&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;segment&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;C&lt;sub&gt;s&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;D&lt;sub&gt;s&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;d&lt;sub&gt;s&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;penalty&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;font color='#b85450'&gt;&lt;b&gt;s1&lt;/b&gt; A&amp;#8211;B&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;4 + 1 FT = &lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+0.25&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;0.094&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;font color='#4d7a38'&gt;&lt;b&gt;s2&lt;/b&gt; A&amp;#8211;C&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&amp;#8722;0.50&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;font color='#b07a00'&gt;&lt;b&gt;s3&lt;/b&gt; B&amp;#8211;C&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;1 FT&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&amp;#8722;0.67&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br&gt;Only s1 is penalised. Its gradient pulls the pins of s1's nets into a single region (fewer A&amp;#8211;B crossings), or slides a crossing along the boundary to another A&amp;#8211;B segment when the pair has one. s2 and s3 feel no force." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="620" y="520" width="520" height="220" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c36" value="&lt;b&gt;Penalty vs utilisation&lt;/b&gt; $$D_s/C_s$$" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=16;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="414" width="420" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c37" value="" style="html=1;endArrow=none;rounded=0;strokeWidth=1;strokeColor=#333333;endArrow=classic;" edge="1" parent="1">
